# plan.md §21.5 item 1. QueryLens is a client-side multi-page app: every route
# except `/` (the stage explainers, `/examples`, and the integrated docs under
# `/docs/*`) is drawn by React Router, not by a file on disk. Without this line
# a hard load of one of those paths — a refresh, a shared link, a new tab —
# matches no asset and Cloudflare serves `404.html`, which carries `noindex`.
# The whole distribution model is a shared link (§14.1, §19.3), so that is the
# deploy-day blocker this closes.
#
# Cloudflare Pages checks static assets before `_redirects`, so `/assets/*`,
# `/fonts/*`, `/og.png`, `/favicon.svg`, `/robots.txt` and the rest still serve
# directly; only unmatched paths fall through to the SPA entry. The 200 keeps
# the requested URL in the address bar (a 301/302 would rewrite it), which is
# what lets React Router read the path it was asked for.
#
# `404.html` is now a last resort only — reached when the app bundle itself
# fails to load, not for ordinary unknown routes, which React Router's `*`
# route renders as `NotFoundPage` inside the loaded app.
